ash: the fallbacks for an old libc, for Linux 2.6.16

The toolchain's glibc defines F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC and O_CLOEXEC, but Linux
2.6.16 predates both (2.6.24 and 2.6.23): fcntl(F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC) fails with
EINVAL, so ash can't run a script ("sh: 3: Invalid argument"), and
O_CLOEXEC is ignored. ash has fallbacks for a libc without them (F_DUPFD,
then FD_CLOEXEC); use those.

--- a/shell/ash.c
+++ b/shell/ash.c
@@ -290,6 +290,8 @@
 # define IF_NOT_FEATURE_SH_STANDALONE(...) __VA_ARGS__
 #endif

+#undef F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC
+#undef O_CLOEXEC
 #ifndef F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC
 # define F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC F_DUPFD
 #endif
